Result: the focused runner passed against three disposable Kafka 4.4.0-SNAPSHOT KRaft brokers and a TCP OffsetCommit response-loss proxy. The existing generic source ACK-loss case passed. The new expiry case forwarded the Grant and Command ACKs, then armed the proxy before the first `EXPIRE_GENERATION` ACK. The Worker returned `ACK_UNKNOWN` for the exact expiry record at offset 2 after the Broker had committed next offset 3; retry ACKed the retained entry without another Store mutation, and duplicate expiry offset 3 advanced the Broker group frontier to 4. The proxy recorded real API key 8 Broker responses as received and not forwarded. The expiry authority resolved once. The E2E script and both smoke invocations exited successfully; the proxy reported 7 dropped responses in the generic case and 8 in the expiry case.

Scope: the signed expiry deliberately targets a missing Message and uses test-only grant, signing, time, and Owner authority fixtures. This run verifies the real three-Broker TCP response-loss boundary and same-Host ACK retry for Target expiry. It does not verify production authority assembly, live Oxia Owner takeover, process-crash recovery at this expiry boundary, migration, or central C1 acceptance.
